# Trivy suppressions
#
# Run locally the way CI does:
#   docker run --rm -v "${PWD}:/repo" aquasec/trivy:latest fs \
#     --scanners vuln,secret,misconfig --severity HIGH,CRITICAL /repo
#
# RULES FOR ADDING AN ENTRY (see docs/security/ci-security-gates.md):
#
#   1. Every entry needs a CVE/AVD id, a one-line reason, an owner, and an
#      expiry date. An undated suppression is a permanent blind spot.
#   2. Suppress only what is genuinely not exploitable here — a vulnerable
#      code path we never call, or a dev-only dependency that never ships.
#      "It's noisy" is not a reason.
#   3. Prefer upgrading. `ignore-unfixed: true` is already set in CI, so
#      anything appearing here HAS a fix available.
#   4. Re-review on expiry. The scheduled Monday scan will resurface it.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-2025-12345 exp:2026-03-01
#   # why: <not exploitable because …>  owner: @jorge
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Active suppressions
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# (none — keep it that way)
